No matter, what character I play, the biggest priority for me is MR, and
the second - reflection.  When I played my monk the last time, it was
neutral, so I wished for The Eye and it was really wonderful. The magic
resistance (without a need to take off the robe) and mana regeneration
(it's just a different class of spellcasting).  The Eye can also save
your life if you realize, that you can't overcome the monsters but still
have some spare HP (would blast you on invocation).   That monk later
succumbed to YASD when he faced the cockatrice with bare hands, but
there is no way it would die a non-YAS death.

About the xorns...  What was the problem?  Did you move too far away
from the magic portal or did you let yourself be surrounded by monsters?
 I can't wiz-test if you can activate the magic portal while standing
there (the ^T in wizmode works as intra-level teleport), but I think,
you can't.  So next time move on the square next to the portal and if
you see, that xorns will overcome you - escape.  Escaping is one of the
most important skills in nethack.


